    "open_questions": [
      "His kit in 1970-73: the Top of the Pops footage shows a grey marbled pearl wrap and chrome, but no maker; the Songsterr tabs name a Ludwig Super Classic in silver sparkle, a Hayman Showman and a Premier without a source.",
      "Which King Crimson drummer he meant ('I loved the drummer'): Michael Giles played on the first album (1969), Andy McCulloch and Ian Wallace after him.",
      "Five Years' opening beat, which he says he wrote: the only Songsterr tab (407348) is a one-bar 6/8 loop that the record does not bear out; transcribe it.",
      "His memoir Spider from Mars (2016) for the playing on each record: not read here."
    ]
  },
