    "roles": ["band_member", "touring", "bandleader"],
    "summary": "David Bowie's drummer from The Man Who Sold the World (1970) to Aladdin Sane (1973), with Mick Ronson and Trevor Bolder the Spiders from Mars: Hunky Dory, Ziggy Stardust and the tour. A rock drummer who loved Bonham and chose to play less ('less-is-more' on Changes), kept a solid beat under Ronson's strings and echoes, and took his rolls in odd places from King Crimson. Dismissed in 1973 (Aynsley Dunbar replaced him); later the Spiders from Mars album, U-Boat, and Holy Holy with Tony Visconti, playing the old records again."
  },
